course: dictionary
lesson: 5564
title: Leo: a name, a star group, a sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Leo starts with a capital letter because it is a name, or a special name for a star group or sign. Read the words around it to know which one it is. «Leo owned up, said sorry, and read the paper aloud to Grandad every morning.» Here Leo is a boy, so it is a name.
explain: Leo can also name a group of stars called the constellation Leo, which is said to look like a lion. In science lessons you can find it in spring in the Northern Hemisphere, with its bright star Regulus. Look for clues such as stars, sky or space to tell that this is the meaning.
explain: Leo can mean a star sign too, for people with birthdays from about 23 July to 22 August. «I'm a Leo» is about a birthday, not about the sky. Star signs are not science, though: the stars do not decide what kind of person you are.
fact: Leo is a constellation, a group of stars said to look like a lion.
fact: The bright star Regulus is in the constellation Leo, which is seen in spring in the Northern Hemisphere.
fact: Leo is the fifth sign of the zodiac, for birthdays from about 23 July to 22 August.
fact: Leo is also a boy's name, and it means «lion» in Latin.
fact: Star signs are not science: the stars do not decide your character.
exercise: «Kai, Priya and Leo decided to build a whole city in Minecraft.» In this sentence, what is Leo? | A star sign for a birthday in August | A kind of pet | *A boy's name | A group of stars
exercise: In a science lesson on space, what is the constellation Leo said to look like? | A fish | A bull | *A lion | A bear
exercise: Which bright star is in the constellation Leo? | *Regulus | Sirius | Betelgeuse | Polaris
test: Someone says «I'm a Leo» and their birthday is in August. What does Leo mean here? | A kind of lion at the zoo | A group of stars seen in spring | A boy's name only | *A star sign for birthdays from about 23 July to 22 August
test: Leo is a Latin word. What does it mean? | Name | *Lion | Star | Sign
exam: Which sentence uses Leo as a name? | The constellation Leo is seen in spring | *«Leo owned up, said sorry, and read the paper aloud to Grandad.» | «I'm a Leo», born in August | Leo means lion in Latin
